            <ArticleTitle>[Synthesis and anti-inflammatory analgesic activities of phenylfuroxan-coupled diclofenac].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>27-32</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="AIM" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To search for new derivatives of diclofenac (DC) having higher potency than the parent drug and lacking its undesirable effects.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">Coupling DC with NO donor 3-hydroxymethyl-4-phenylfuroxan and its isomer through esterification, evaluating anti-inflammatory and analgesic activities, observing side effects in the rat gastrointestinal (GI) tract and assessing NO releasing ability both in vitro and in vivo.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">Fifteen new compounds including nine target ones (II1-9) were synthesized, and their structures were determined by IR, 1HNMR, MS and elemental analysis. Compounds II3 and II9 showed anti-inflammatory activity comparable to DC. Compound II2 showed stronger anti-inflammatory and analgesic activities and less GI side effect than DC, and released NO in vivo.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Compound II2 is worthy to be intensively studied.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
